    "result_text": "All 32 tests pass, including the new `Cp21Tests`. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required emitting an audit line via the `AUDIT` logger on successful owner create, carrying the owner id, customerCode and registrationDate.\n\nI added a new function step to the `POST /api/owners` pipeline:\n\n- **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** (`src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 a single-method function that reads the owner via `@Val Owner` and logs through `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`, including the id, customerCode and registrationDate.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `audit` step between `save` and `respond` (`save \u2192 audit \u2192 respond`), under the same `transaction` governance. Placing it after `save` ensures the owner has its generated id; customerCode and registrationDate are already assigned earlier in the pipeline.\n\nThe audit line format (`owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-24`) contains all three values as substrings, satisfying the test's `anyContains(id, customerCode, registrationDate)` assertion \u2014 and `LocalDate.toString()` yields the same ISO form the JSON response serializes.",
